**Q2.** An integer array is initialized as A= [10, 9, 2, 19, 23, 32, 4, 7, 46, 18]. Write the updated values of the array after the function *fun* (...) is executed; low & high are leftmost & rightmost indexes of A.  
****

```cpp
int fun (vector <int>&A, int low, int high)
{
    int p= A[high]
    int i= low-1:
    for (int j=low; j<high; ++j)
    {
        if (A[j] <=p)
        {
            ++i;
            swap (A [i], A[j]);
        }
    }
    swap (A [i+1], A[high])
    return i+1;
}
```
